The issue "proxy isatty" suggests that when `rich` attempts to check if a file stream (like `sys.stdout`) is a TTY using `isatty()`, it fails or behaves unexpectedly when the stream is wrapped by `FileProxy`.

In `rich/file_proxy.py`, `FileProxy` delegates all attribute access to the wrapped file object (`self.__file`) via `__getattr__`. If `isatty()` is called on `FileProxy`, it calls `getattr(self.__file, "isatty")`.

To fix this, `FileProxy` should implement `isatty()` itself, delegating the call to the underlying file object, ensuring that any code expecting a file-like object with an `isatty` method receives a consistent implementation, even if the underlying object doesn't expose it directly or if the proxy needs to manage the check.

I will add an `isatty` method to `FileProxy` in `rich/file_proxy.py`.

