    def __getattr__(self, name: str) -> Any:
        return getattr(self.__file, name)
```

I will modify this to include `isatty`.

```python
    def __getattr__(self, name: str) -> Any:
        if name == "isatty":
            return getattr(self.__file, "isatty")
        return getattr(self.__file, name)
```
Wait, if I just add it to `__getattr__`, it's redundant if `self.__file` already has it. The issue is likely that `isatty` might not be available on `self.__file` in all contexts, or the proxy needs to handle the check itself.

